// @check
// @error print of a union value ("ab" | i32) is type-valid but not yet supported by codegen
// CONTRACT (must-error): a union of a string LITERAL and a scalar is the boxed value union
// `string|i32` once the emitter softens the literal (`canonEmitName`: "a mixed-base union
// keeps each softened member"), so `print` cannot lower it — exactly as it cannot lower the
// already-softened spelling `string | i32` (tests/cases/types/print-union-rejected.vl).
//
// Before D-LITPRINT the two spellings DISAGREED: `string | i32` was rejected here while
// `"ab" | i32` walked past the gate and built a module that failed to parse as WebAssembly
// (`type mismatch: expected i32, found (ref $type)`). The gate classified each leaf with
// `retAtomKindOf`, which answers -1 for a literal, and one -1 leaf declined the whole union.
const v: "ab" | i32 = 3
print(v)
